(5808073, 844120, 51379, '<td valign="top">Well done nice panorama, I know its really tough to get a shot of the moon when its behind the clouds...good luck!</td>', 'Well done nice panorama, I know its really tough to get a shot of the moon when its behind the clouds...good luck!', '2010-01-12 19:42:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(5808084, 845071, 51379, '<td valign="top">This shot really has all it takes for a perfect shot your settings are near perfect, I would have maybe waited momentarily until the clouds moved slightly for a slightly brighter moon and possibly then cropped it a little tighter so that the moon was maybe a little larger and taking some of the blank black portion out. then possibly allowing the moon to be closer to the "rule of thirds"( not that that is always the answer) but may have worked a little better here. I know that often when we crop tighter /closer to the subject our images seem to get "noisier" however, a little more noise may have been tolerable in order to get the impact of a larger moon! Good Luck here!</td>', 'This shot really has all it takes for a perfect shot your settings are near perfect, I would have maybe waited momentarily until the clouds moved slightly for a slightly brighter moon and possibly then cropped it a little tighter so that the moon was maybe a little larger and taking some of the blank black portion out. then possibly allowing the moon to be closer to the "rule of thirds"( not that that is always the answer) but may have worked a little better here. I know that often when we crop tighter /closer to the subject our images seem to get "noisier" however, a little more noise may have been tolerable in order to get the impact of a larger moon! Good Luck here!', '2010-01-12 19:58:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5808086, 844909, 51379, '<td valign="top">...I know mines not blue either! nice sharp shot though!</td>', '...I know mines not blue either! nice sharp shot though!', '2010-01-12 20:01:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5808114, 844350, 51379, '<td valign="top">This is quite nice.... I''ve been to the bridge a few times and its ALWAYS fogged in, this past september I hardly even saw any of it.<br/> More detail in the moon could have come from a slightly faster shutter to cut back on the light, possibly cutting back on the blown-out blended street lights lower right  but maintain your obvious high f-stop in order to maintain depth of detail.that shutter speed will darken the rest of the shot but then, selectively   lighten the rest of the shot in p.p. This is a really tough shot without having post processing. Good Luck here!</td>', 'This is quite nice.... I''ve been to the bridge a few times and its ALWAYS fogged in, this past september I hardly even saw any of it. More detail in the moon could have come from a slightly faster shutter to cut back on the light, possibly cutting back on the blown-out blended street lights lower right  but maintain your obvious high f-stop in order to maintain depth of detail.that shutter speed will darken the rest of the shot but then, selectively   lighten the rest of the shot in p.p. This is a really tough shot without having post processing. Good Luck here!', '2010-01-12 20:18:12.000000', NULL, 1),
